<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-3240] Arrays do not deserialize properly</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-3240</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Code to reproduce:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;IgniteCache&amp;lt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;Integer&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;[]&amp;gt; cache = ignite.getOrCreateCache(CACHE_NAME);
cache.put(1, &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;[]{&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;hello&quot;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;world&quot;&lt;/span&gt;});
&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;[] res = cache.get(1);
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The bug is in CacheObjectContext.unwrapBinariesInArrayIfNeeded method, which always produces a new array.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We should check for basic types somehow and skip this conversion.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Generally, we NEVER want to change the type of the array, so the fix may be:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (arr.getClass().getComponentType() != &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;Object&lt;/span&gt;.class)
    &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; arr;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
